{
  "$description": "The design tokens of Forever Sixty: the only hand-edited token file (design/specs/2026-11-07-mobile-redesign.md section 2.1), in the W3C design-tokens format. node design/tokens/build.mjs writes web/src/styles/tokens.css, apps/ios/Shared/DesignTokens.swift and the Android Tokens.kt from it; design/tokens/tokens.test.mjs fails on a stale output. The extension gg.foreversixty carries what the outputs need: css (the custom property a token defines on the web; a token without one is not on the web), cssAliases (properties that read it through var()), native (false: not in the apps; ios or android: one app only), wide (the value from 1760 px, data-column wide), phone (the value below 768 px on the web, and the apps' value), platformValue (a per-app value), flatten (a group whose name the native identifiers leave out), and per type role its css properties, scalesWith (the iOS Dynamic Type style) and tabular. Native identifiers are the token path after its top group in camelCase (color.class.warrior is FSColor.classWarrior); a path that would start with a digit takes the top group's name (space.4 is FSSpace.space4).",
